Apple has renewed its popular British spy drama "Slow Horses" for ninth and tenth seasons, extending its considerable lead as <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a>'s longest-running original series by season, according to <a href="https://deadline.com/2026/11/slow-horses-seasons-9-10-apple-tv-1237225018/"><em>Deadline</em></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/slow-horses.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1077564" /><br/>
Six seasons of Slow Horses have already been released, with seasons seven and eight already confirmed before the latest renewal. The order for seasons nine and ten extends its lead as the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; original with the most seasons commissioned.<br/>
<br/>
The commitment puts "Slow Horses" well ahead of other established Apple originals. "For All Mankind," which debuted when the service launched in 2019, will <a href="https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/news/2026/03/apple-tv-renews-award-winning-and-globally-acclaimed-space-drama-for-all-mankind-for-sixth-and-final-season/">finish with season six</a>. <br/>
<br/>
"Slow Horses" has also maintained an exceptional critical reception, with all six seasons holding critics' scores of 95% or higher on <a href="https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/slow_horses">Rotten Tomatoes</a>. Seasons two and four have perfect 100% ratings, while the latest season holds 98%.<br/>
<br/>
The news answers recent uncertainty about the show's future. Cast member Olivia Cooke had suggested just days earlier that season eight could mark its conclusion.<br/>
<br/>
The television series is catching up with the book series it is based on that began 16 years ago. Author Mick Herron has published nine main "Slough House" novels since the first one debuted in 2010, with gaps of between one and three years between installments. The latest, "Clown Town," arrived in 2025, three years after "Bad Actors."<br/>
<br/>
Those two books provide the material for seasons seven and eight, raising the possibility that seasons nine and ten could move beyond the published novels. Apple has not confirmed that direction, with a spokesperson telling <em>Deadline</em> that story details for the additional seasons would follow.<br/>
<br/>
